Law texts

The texts in this repository are the Acts, Ordinances and Regulations of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa (Pakistan) as published
in revised form on the Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Code (kpcode.kp.gov.pk) by the Law, Parliamentary Affairs and Human Rights
Department, Government of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa ("© 2026 Law & Parliamentary Affairs Department, Government of KP").
The site states no licence for reuse.

- Copyright: the Copyright Ordinance, 1962 (Ordinance No. XXXIV of 1962), s. 57(1) begins "The following acts shall
  not constitute an infringement of copyright, namely:" and clause (q) reads: "the reproduction or publication of__
  (i) any matter which has been published in any official Gazette, or the report of any committee, commission,
  council, board or other like body appointed by the Government unless the reproduction or publication of such
  matter or report is prohibited by the Government". The laws of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa are published in the Khyber
  Pakhtunkhwa Gazette, and no prohibition by the Government of reproducing them was found. The texts are reproduced
  without change to their wording; only the arrangement (one file per section or Schedule, one paragraph per line)
  is Lexifina's.
- Limits of that basis: the KP Code's revised texts are the department's consolidation, and their footnotes (kept in
  data/amendments.csv) are the department's wording. Section 57(1)(q)(i) covers matter published in the Gazette; it
  does not in terms cover the consolidation and footnotes, which record facts (which law changed which words).
- The site says: "This site is developed only for informational purposes and is subject to the Disclaimer." The
  texts are not the authoritative text: the laws as published in the Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Gazette are.

